# Packages removed when policy mode KIOSK is applied.
#
# READ D12 BEFORE EDITING THIS FILE. We are not building a minimal image. We are removing the
# BINARIES A USER COULD REACH A DESKTOP THROUGH from the one base we have, and leaving the shared
# libraries the dependency closure will not release. That is a deliberate trade of image size for the
# one-rebuild CVE property, and the real measured size is reported rather than a minimal one we did
# not achieve. See policy/README.md, "what kiosk costs you".
#
# THIS LIST IS NOT THE POST-CONDITION. absent-binaries.list is. A package name can change, split or
# be renamed upstream overnight; the binary a student would use to get a desktop cannot hide from
# `command -v`. apply-policy removes what is here and then FAILS THE BUILD if anything in
# absent-binaries.list is still on the image. Check S9 asserts the same thing independently.
#
# Missing packages are not an error -- they are logged and skipped. Upstream moves.

# ---- the desktop shell itself -------------------------------------------------------------------
plasma-workspace
plasma-workspace-wayland
plasma-workspace-x11
plasma-desktop
plasma-session
gnome-shell
gnome-session
gnome-session-wayland-session

# ---- display managers: the other way to a desktop ------------------------------------------------
sddm
sddm-x11
sddm-wayland-plasma
sddm-wayland-generic
sddm-kcm
gdm
lightdm
lightdm-gtk

# ---- terminal emulators: a window with a shell in it is a way out --------------------------------
konsole
konsole5
xterm
gnome-terminal
alacritty
kitty
foot

# ---- desktop applications that are file managers, software installers or system editors ----------
# Each of these is a door: browse the filesystem, install something, edit a unit, read a log.
dolphin
plasma-discover
plasma-discover-notifier
plasma-discover-flatpak
plasma-discover-packagekit
gnome-software
nautilus
kate
kwrite
plasma-systemmonitor
ksysguard
kinfocenter
systemsettings
plasma-welcome
kde-partitionmanager
gparted
